course: dictionary
lesson: 10750
title: Urge: a strong push to act
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To urge someone is to try hard to persuade them, or to tell them strongly that they should do something. «Police urge drivers to slow down» means the police are strongly asking drivers to go more slowly. Urge can be a verb or a noun.
explain: An urge is a strong wish or need to do something, often one that comes suddenly. «Even well-fed pet cats still feel the urge to chase and pounce» means the wish to chase is strong, even when the cat is not hungry. Look for clues like strong, sudden and need.
explain: Context tells you which meaning to use. «Run!» urged the captain, and the team ran faster. Here urge means to strongly tell someone to do something. When you urge an animal on, you push it to move faster, so urge is a little like a gentle push.
fact: Urge can be a verb (to urge, urges, urged, urging) or a noun (an urge, urges).
fact: To urge someone is to try hard to persuade them, or to strongly tell them they should do something.
fact: An urge is a strong wish or need to do something, often one that comes suddenly.
fact: «Impulse» is a close synonym: an impulse is a sudden urge to act, so «practising a pause gives you more control over impulses».
fact: Useful phrases: «urge someone to», «have an urge to», «a sudden urge», «resist the urge», «urge on».
exercise: «Police urge drivers to slow down.» What does urge mean here? | Lose control | Drive past quickly | Shout very loudly | *Strongly ask or persuade
exercise: «Even well-fed pet cats still feel the urge to chase.» What is an urge? | A small, quiet sound | A sleepy feeling after a meal | *A strong wish or need to do something | A kind of food for cats
exercise: Which phrase means to stop yourself from giving in to a strong wish? | Urge someone to laugh | Have an urge to | *Resist the urge | Urge on
test: Mum says, «I urge you to wear your helmet.» What is Mum doing? | Forgetting about the helmet | *Strongly persuading you to do it | Asking if you own a helmet | Pushing you off your bike
test: «The dog had a sudden urge to chase the ball.» What does a sudden urge show? | *A quick, strong wish to do something | A sound the dog makes | A ball that has been lost | A slow, tired feeling
exam: In «a sudden urge to laugh», what kind of word is urge? | Adverb | *Noun | Adjective | Verb
